speechtext:
The house resumed, from Wednesday, August 5, consideration in committee of the following resolution-Mr. Mcllraith-Mr. La-moureux in the chair.
Resolved, that a sum not exceeding $696,010,791.01, being the aggregate of-
(a)	two twelfths of the total of all of the items set forth in the main estimates for the fiscal year ending 31 March, 1965, laid before the House of Commons at the present session of parliament $658,598,418.50;
(b)	an additional three twelfths of the amount of transport items 15 and 25, (schedule A) of the said main estimates, $7,044,425;
(c)	an additional one twelfth of the amount of agriculture item 60, fisheries item 20, justice item 1, legislation item 20, mines and technical surveys items 10, 15, 25, 45 and 60, national film board item 1, national health and welfare item 15, northern affairs and national resources items 15 and 35,
Interim Supply
privy council item 25, transport item 1, loans, investments and advances item L10 (schedule B) of the said main estimates, $9,525,758.34;
(d)	two twelfths of all the items to be voted in the supplementary estimates (A) laid before the House of Commons at the present session of parliament, except national defence 56a, loans, investments and advances items L17a and L37a, for which no proportion will be granted, $20,840,372.50;
(e)	an additional two twelfths of the amount of justice item 12a (schedule C) of the said supplementary estimates (A), $1,806.67;
be granted to Her Majesty on account of the fiscal year ending 31 March, 1965.

Put it in Hansard.
[Editor's Note: The text of the resolution in substitution above referred to is as follows:]
Resolved, that a sum not exceeding $1,037,030,109.84, being the aggregate of-
(a)	three twelfths of the total of all the items set forth in the main estimates for the fiscal year ending 31st March, 1965, laid before the House of Commons at the present session of parliament except external affairs item 20, for which the proportion is two twelfths, $987,817,169.42;
Interim Supply
(b)	an additional three twelfths of the amount of transport items 15 and 25. (schedule A) of the said main estimates, $7,044,425;
(c)	an additional two twelfths of the amount of agriculture item 60, legislation item 20, (schedule B) of the said main estimates, $4,235,450;
(d)	an additional one twelfth of the amount of agriculture item 25, fisheries item 20, mines and technical surveys items 10, 15, 25 , 45 and 60, national film board item 1, northern affairs and national resources items 15 and 35, privy council item 25, transport item 1, loans, investments and advances item L110, (schedule C) of the said main estimates, $6,442,850;
(e)	three twelfths of all the items to be voted in the supplementary estimates (A) laid before the House of Commons at the present session of Parliament, except national defence item 56a and loans, investments and advances items L17a and L37a, for which no proportion will be granted, $31,260,558.75;
(f)	an additional two twelfths of the amount of justice item 12a and loans, investments and advances item L12a, (schedule D) of the said supplementary estimates (A), $229,656.67;
be granted to Her Majesty on account of the fiscal year ending 31st March, 1965.
